  "limitations": "Only Linux main.lua now passes in both standalone engines. All full-entry audits retain nonzero exits: common Windows main.lua:53 failure; Linux C big.lua:11 assertion; Linux Rust missing POSIX locales. Stock mode does not provide the internal T module or suite native libraries, so automatically skipped tests are unproven. Source hashes and assertions are unchanged. Full standalone Lua 5.1, complete C/auxiliary APIs, production native loading, broader GC/debug/resource behavior, later dialects and integrations remain open. Baseline checkouts had recorded CRLF conversions; final builds use exact workspace bytes. No performance tuning or benchmarks accompany this milestone."
